      "kind": "configuration",
      "necessary": true,
      "established": true,
      "requirement": "Parser hashing on the target's parse and external-entity surface must be able to use a full 16-byte salt from a supported high-quality source, through XML_SetHashSalt16Bytes before parsing or Expat's automatic generation.",
      "target_route": "LLVMFuzzerTestOneInput creates root and namespace parsers, then calls ParseOneInput, which derives an unsigned-long SipHash value from the input, calls XML_SetHashSalt, and calls XML_Parse. It later creates, parses, and frees two child parsers.",
      "failure_condition": "For a finite valid XML input whose derived salt is nonzero, XML_SetHashSalt sets the upper key word to zero, writes only the unsigned-long value to the lower word, and sets the salt flag. XML_Parse therefore skips automatic full-salt generation, and internal hashing uses the limited key.",
      "alternative_paths": "The namespace parser uses the same helper. Children inherit the parent's salt and flag and also use that helper. No parser route calls XML_SetHashSalt16Bytes. A zero derived salt can leave automatic generation available, but it does not satisfy the full-salt requirement for the nonzero-salt condition assessed here.",
